1
00:00:00,459 --> 00:00:02,159
(Howard:)I don't know.
It's pretty catchy.

2
00:00:02,160 --> 00:00:03,760
(Penny:)Do you even like the Beach Boys?

3
00:00:03,762 --> 00:00:05,732
They have "beach"
right in the name.

4
00:00:05,731 --> 00:00:08,101
(Sheldon:)What do you think?

5
00:00:08,100 --> 00:00:10,430
(Leonard:)Well, now that you can focus
again, what do you say

6
00:00:10,435 --> 00:00:12,365
(Leonard:)we get back to surface tension
of domain walls?

7
00:00:12,371 --> 00:00:15,041
(Sheldon:)Of course. I'm already
seeing a more efficient way

8
00:00:15,040 --> 00:00:17,370
(Sheldon:)of taming the ultravi...

9
00:00:17,376 --> 00:00:19,806
(Sheldon:)I know why
the song was in my head.

10
00:00:19,811 --> 00:00:22,381
(Howard:)Why?
It's about Amy.

11
00:00:22,381 --> 00:00:24,751
(Penny:)Okay, look, I know
Amy's like an old lady,

12
00:00:24,750 --> 00:00:26,920
(Penny:)but she's not old enough
to have a song

13
00:00:26,918 --> 00:00:29,018
from the '60s written about her.

14
00:00:29,020 --> 00:00:31,050
(Sheldon:)It's about
how she made my life better.

15
00:00:31,056 --> 00:00:32,426
(Sheldon:)Consider the lyrics.

16
00:00:32,424 --> 00:00:34,594
"I was living like half a man.

17
00:00:34,593 --> 00:00:37,063
"Then I couldn't love,
but now I can.

18
00:00:37,062 --> 00:00:38,262
"More soul than

19
00:00:38,263 --> 00:00:39,263
"I ever had.

20
00:00:39,264 --> 00:00:41,834
(Sheldon:)I love the way
you soften my life."

21
00:00:41,833 --> 00:00:44,773
Well, she did soften your life,
didn't she?

22
00:00:44,770 --> 00:00:46,140
Yes!

23
00:00:46,138 --> 00:00:48,708
(Sheldon:)She's like
the dryer sheets of my heart!

24
00:00:51,109 --> 00:00:52,309
(Sheldon:)I have to go.

25
00:00:54,513 --> 00:00:56,443
